WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.717
DeepMind lets AI

00:00:01.529 --> 00:00:02.873
agents control part

00:00:02.685 --> 00:00:03.604
of its compute

00:00:04.134 --> 00:00:05.454
On Google DeepMind's

00:00:05.266 --> 00:00:06.091
podcast

00:00:06.221 --> 00:00:07.530
Gemini lead Koray

00:00:07.342 --> 00:00:09.181
Kavukcuoglu said agents

00:00:08.992 --> 00:00:10.254
now run experiments

00:00:10.066 --> 00:00:10.855
on their own

00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:11.457
with part of

00:00:11.268 --> 00:00:12.353
the lab's compute

00:00:12.886 --> 00:00:14.395
Kavukcuoglu describes

00:00:14.207 --> 00:00:15.114
a shift from

00:00:14.926 --> 00:00:16.176
separate specialist

00:00:15.987 --> 00:00:16.954
teams to one

00:00:16.766 --> 00:00:18.015
general-purpose model

00:00:17.827 --> 00:00:18.982
line for science

00:00:18.794 --> 00:00:19.737
and products

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:21.117
with each Gemini

00:00:20.928 --> 00:00:22.343
generation a hand-built

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:22.838
one-off

00:00:22.969 --> 00:00:24.336
while parallel teams

00:00:24.148 --> 00:00:25.480
work on successors

00:00:26.006 --> 00:00:26.890
As a safety

00:00:26.702 --> 00:00:27.338
measure

00:00:27.492 --> 00:00:28.588
DeepMind does not

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.461
reward the agents'

00:00:29.272 --> 00:00:30.097
chain of thought

00:00:29.909 --> 00:00:30.782
during training

00:00:30.947 --> 00:00:31.878
so their reasoning

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:33.175
stays unfiltered and

00:00:32.987 --> 00:00:34.178
reviewable before they

00:00:33.989 --> 00:00:34.567
act

00:00:35.094 --> 00:00:36.108
Full story on

00:00:35.919 --> 00:00:36.815
the dashboard
